First paper: Acyclic identification of aptamers for human alpha-thrombin using over-represented libraries and deep sequencing; https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0019395 

This one is novel because in the methods section it described in detail the modified SELEX process they used to develop aptamers, whose sequences they reported. Specifically the paper described the process of looking for a thrombin aptamer, finding the Carb1 aptamer and discovering its potential as a hexose aptamer

Second Paper: Probing the limits of aptamer affinity with a microfluidic SELEX platform
https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0027051 

This one is novel because they also describe in detail the process of finding aptamers for Thrombin, alongside other model targets, and report a sequence for alpha thrombin that they describe as novel. 
